#
# The built-in keyboard back after a wake. Some machines' firmware turns the
# keyboard controller off as the lid closes and does not turn it on again
# after deep sleep (S3): the keyboard is dead until the machine is folded into
# a tablet and back. Re-attaching Linux's keyboard driver sends it the
# commands that turn it on. Lighter sleep (s2idle) also kept the keyboard, but
# on the same machine left the screen black and touch dead after a wake.
#
# Installed by hand where it is needed, as root:
#   install -m 755 setup/system-sleep/talaris-keyboard /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/
# systemd runs it with "pre" before sleep and "post" after; only "post" acts.

[ "$1" = post ] || exit 0
driver=/sys/bus/serio/drivers/atkbd
[ -e "$driver/serio0" ] || exit 0
printf serio0 > "$driver/unbind"
printf serio0 > "$driver/bind"
